From db1b3dc8cef4e6f7e6fff8e419d1b24f9617b029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Dugan <patrick.buchanan.dugan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:02:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Swap payload bridge: positional fields, data envelope,
 expiry and listener capability

- rpc-proxy builds tl4 commits from [propertyId, amount, channelAddress, ...] and
  tl3 trades from [propertyId, tokens, native, expiryBlock, columnA, tokenOutput,
  payToAddress] as nine parts, returns { data }, and errors on any missing field
  instead of defaulting (the legacy four-argument trade call is refused).
- The seller passes the negotiated channel address; both sides take the column
  from the listener; the trade pins token delivery to output 0 and payment to
  output 1, and the PSBT guard refuses those outputs elsewhere.
- Each side checks tl_getProtocolCapabilities first: the seller before its
  commit, the buyer before building the trade.
- The bridge probe now decodes through the candidate decoder and exits 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
